course: dictionary
lesson: 3597
title: Fiercely and how strongly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fiercely is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. In «The lion roared fiercely», the clue is roared: a lion's roar is loud and wild, so fiercely means in a wild, angry way.
explain: Fiercely can also mean very strongly, with great feeling. «Mum is fiercely proud of my painting» does not mean she is angry. It means she is very, very proud. The words around it show which meaning fits.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "in a wild way" or "very strongly". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Fiercely» means in an angry, wild or violent way, or very strongly with great feeling.
fact: The root word is «fierce», so a fierce dog barks, and a dog that barks fiercely does it in a fierce way.
fact: «Geese defend their nests fiercely», so they guard their nests with great force.
fact: «A hippo guards its water so fiercely» means it protects its water very strongly, and this is why hippos are dangerous to people in Africa.
fact: Many adverbs end in -ly, and this is a clue. Changing fierce to fiercely turns a describing word into a word that tells how.
exercise: «The wind blew fiercely across the bay all night.» How did the wind blow? | *Strongly and wildly | Gently, like a summer breeze | Quietly, under the door | Slowly and softly
exercise: Lily says, «Mum is fiercely proud of my painting.» What does fiercely mean here? | Without any care at all | *Very strongly, with great feeling | Very quickly | Angrily, with a shout
exercise: «Geese defend their nests fiercely.» Which word tells you how they defend their nests? | *fiercely | nests | geese | defend
test: «A hippo guards its water so fiercely that it is dangerous to people.» What does fiercely mean here? | *Very strongly, with great force | Happily, with a song | Slowly, like a sleepy animal | Quietly, so no one hears
test: «Ella is fiercely independent.» What does fiercely add to the meaning? | *She is very strongly independent, and likes doing things herself | She is too tired to try | She is angry and shouts at everyone | She is sleepy and slow
exam: «Colonists were given the right to labour, and the friar wrote fiercely against its cruelty.» What does fiercely tell us about how he wrote? | About a happy day | Very slowly, with a soft pencil | Very quietly, in a tiny hand | *With strong feeling and determination
